ives a homomorphism and omits strictness; the theorem does not. **Theorem:** yes — `nonempty_algHom_of_continuousOnMaps` is existence of a strict homomorphism out of an isomorphic algebra into every algebra with strict structure map, which is the theorem in the strict category of Definition 6.8. **Proof:** yes — strictness of the inverse, the approximable witness for \(T\), the least fixed point of \(h\mapsto k\circ T(h)\circ j\), and the cancellation of \(j\circ i\) are the printed rewrite.
